  "kind": "process",
  "title": "Domestication of sugarcane",
  "summary": "Sugarcane was domesticated from the wild species Saccharum robustum in New Guinea and nearby islands, around 8,000 years ago by one study and around 8000 BC by another. People may have selected it as a sweeter chewing plant. It later reached Southeast Asia and India, where crystallized sugar was invented in the fifth century AD. Cultivation and refining then spread to China, Persia and the Mediterranean, and sugarcane reached Spain around 715 AD.",
